{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"37e263511549d804","type":"text","text":"A dwarven man 350 years old, he lives within the All-Hammers will.\n\nDressed in robes of deep orange and black, signifying the colours of The All-Hammer. Burvano is a kinda man who is stoic in nature and giving to his people. \n","x":-220,"y":-40,"width":525,"height":150},
		{"id":"c217aa00731a67b8","type":"text","text":"[[Saggnus Wildbottom.canvas]]\n#NPC ","x":-345,"y":-180,"width":250,"height":55},
		{"id":"aa7f92e407a514ea","x":-345,"y":200,"width":725,"height":440,"type":"text","text":"The Yormindars and history of Yormindars founding.\n\nYormindar was founded by Bondrick Yormindar under the guidance of Moradin. In the year 10 P.D Moradin knew he would have to protect and hide his once great forge near the center of the realm and its only path way. This forge rests at the very bottom of what is now know as the residuum mines, on the lowest layer of the mines rests a forge made entirely of Dark Silver which is the strongest ore Moradin ever made. This forge holds the secrets and necessary tools to use the ore to manufacture the weapons known as the Vestiges of Divergence, because of this Moradin made his decision to bury both it and the vestige he created at the bottom of his home the mountain named Yormindar. This is where Bondrick came in, he was to create a city within the mountain and mine the surrounding residuum all while protecting the forge below bestowing him with the name Yormindar. Bondrick was the most accomplished craftsmen of all those who followed Moradin during the Divergence which is the reason he was selected for this honor. Upon his selection Bondrick asked for the aid of a great mage who the name of is lost in time. This mage placed a seal on The Forge of Moradin that is nearly unbreakable and on the same day they opened a rift to the plane of fire on one of the upper layers bringing forth fire giants that fled to escape a fire dragon. That is the story of the creation of Yormindar.\n"},
		{"id":"a6642cfd3e41a40c","x":440,"y":200,"width":763,"height":401,"type":"text","text":"The wildbottoms relation to the Yormindars:\n\nSaggnus Sr is a cousin of the Yormindar family,his father named Yorgan fell in love with a woman from wildmount and had a child with her however their relationship was secret and he could not let anyone know he had a child because he did not want to burden him with the responsibilities of the Yormindar family, protecting the forge. \n\nSaggnus Sr. was curious why he never knew his father and went into the bottom of the residuum mines because he was given a vision of a ring within the City of Giants that could grant him the power to release the seal on a vault containing secret information about his family. In desperation he found the ring and began wearing it, over time it became clear that this ring was corrupting him and changing the man he was to something sinister. This ring holds a direct link to the underworld and was placed there by someone or something in hopes to corrupt the mind of a Yormindar and force them to release the seal opening the forge to the possible take over of evil. When Saggnus Sr found this out he attempted to dispose of the ring but he couldn’t and after sharing this with Burvano he disappeared within a few days and the ring alongside him. \n"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}